    <string name="pif_footer_title">Passing basic integrity</string>
    <string name="pif_footer_body">A Canary fingerprint is fetched and refreshed automatically every 21 days. Canary configs expire roughly 6 weeks from their release date — the expiry is shown in the active config summary.\n\nFor manual setup:\n1. Tap \"Fetch Pixel Canary fingerprint\" and select a device.\n2. If no devices are found, import a working PIF config from a trusted source. Config files are not provided.\n3. Recheck your Play Integrity status.\n\nAlways delete the active configuration before importing a new one. Loading an expired PIF config will cause TrickyStore strong integrity to fail even with a valid keybox.\n\nAdvanced spoofing:\n• Play Store fingerprint spoof — leave disabled unless advised otherwise. Spoofing FINGERPRINT to Play Store is rarely needed and may cause issues.\n• Spoof SDK to DroidGuard — forces the legacy pre-Android 13 attestation path. Only enable this if basic integrity is failing and your config targets an older SDK.</string>
